record jpegxl-rs.evidence.phase4f-bytes-unchanged-2026-08-10/1 : evidence {
    title "At 08e67ef the corpus fingerprints are unchanged by the search elision. Default effort: small_0p8MP 1,075,465 B sha16 C3C60CEE4D0741D9 in 240 ms, mid_4MP 5,157,974 B sha16 5C49AB9020706F0D in 470 ms, large_12MP 9,795,599 B sha16 CA27799D3E7B441D in 1008 ms -- all three IDENTICAL to the pre-4E fingerprints, so 4F changed no byte at the default. Effort 7 likewise reproduces all three fingerprints (1207 / 5366 / 15646 ms), confirming the elision does not fire on the density anchor. Separately, jpxl bench modular --iters 3 at 12 MP reports the median falling from 1025.6 ms to 873.5 ms (-14.8%) with diag residual_scans 1 -> 0 and plane_clone_bytes 288,000,000 -> 144,000,000: the skipped work was the RCT scoring copy, the Arc wrap of every plane, and one strided residual scan."
    state verified
    result pass
    method command
    observed_at git:08e67ef11742aefb93158e27fc997d7f646583a2
    command "pwsh -NoProfile -File .agent/scratch/effort-ramp-2026-08-10/verify_default_flip.ps1"
    summary """
        At 08e67ef the corpus fingerprints are unchanged by the search elision. Default effort: small_0p8MP 1,075,465 B sha16 C3C60CEE4D0741D9 in 240 ms, mid_4MP 5,157,974 B sha16 5C49AB9020706F0D in 470 ms, large_12MP 9,795,599 B sha16 CA27799D3E7B441D in 1008 ms -- all three IDENTICAL to the pre-4E fingerprints, so 4F changed no byte at the default. Effort 7 likewise reproduces all three fingerprints (1207 / 5366 / 15646 ms), confirming the elision does not fire on the density anchor. Separately, jpxl bench modular --iters 3 at 12 MP reports the median falling from 1025.6 ms to 873.5 ms (-14.8%) with diag residual_scans 1 -> 0 and plane_clone_bytes 288,000,000 -> 144,000,000: the skipped work was the RCT scoring copy, the Arc wrap of every plane, and one strided residual scan.
        """
    author "GitHub Uploader"
}

record jpegxl-rs.evidence.phase4f-elision-equivalent-2026-08-10/1 : evidence {
    title "At 08e67ef the jpxl-encode library suite is 117 passed, 0 failed, 0 ignored -- 115 pre-4F plus the two gates this work added. degenerate_budget_plans_what_the_full_search_would_have runs plan_for (which short-circuits) and plan_by_full_search (forced past the short-circuit via FullSearchProbe::ForegoneBudget) on the same 37x29 structured input, for every effort level whose budget is a foregone conclusion, crossed with both rct polarities and 1- and 3-channel inputs, and asserts the two plans agree on group_size_shift, rct, squeeze, palette presence, leaf predictors, context count and depth. the_default_effort_reaches_the_short_circuit asserts the elision fires at Effort::DEFAULT and does not fire at level 7, so a future budget edit that silently restores the skipped work fails the suite rather than passing quietly."
    state verified
    result pass
    method command
    observed_at git:08e67ef11742aefb93158e27fc997d7f646583a2
    command "cargo test -p jpxl-encode --lib"
    summary """
        At 08e67ef the jpxl-encode library suite is 117 passed, 0 failed, 0 ignored -- 115 pre-4F plus the two gates this work added. degenerate_budget_plans_what_the_full_search_would_have runs plan_for (which short-circuits) and plan_by_full_search (forced past the short-circuit via FullSearchProbe::ForegoneBudget) on the same 37x29 structured input, for every effort level whose budget is a foregone conclusion, crossed with both rct polarities and 1- and 3-channel inputs, and asserts the two plans agree on group_size_shift, rct, squeeze, palette presence, leaf predictors, context count and depth. the_default_effort_reaches_the_short_circuit asserts the elision fires at Effort::DEFAULT and does not fire at level 7, so a future budget edit that silently restores the skipped work fails the suite rather than passing quietly.
        """
    author "GitHub Uploader"
}

record jpegxl-rs.evidence.phase4g-bound-and-identity-tests-2026-08-10/1 : evidence {
    title "At 2b7b5c0 the jpxl-encode library suite is 122 passed, 0 failed, 0 ignored -- 117 pre-4G plus five gates this work added. bounded_budget_is_a_noop_below_the_budget asserts that for every shipped effort level a frame inside the budget scores at the floor stride, including the exact boundary, so the plumbing cannot change output on sub-budget frames. bounded_budget_raises_the_stride_with_frame_size asserts the stride rises with frame size and that scored samples stay within the budget plus at most two partial rows -- slack that is a function of row cost, not frame area, which is the property that makes ranking cost frame-size-independent. a_zero_budget_falls_back_to_the_floor_stride pins the degenerate cases. empty_overrides_leave_every_effort_budget_untouched and each_override_replaces_only_its_own_lever pin the measurement escape hatch as inert by default. Separately verified: the one workspace failure, both_oracles_decode_a_stream_from_the_hf_mul_segment in jpxl-encode-policy/tests/vardct_oracle.rs, is pre-existing -- it fails identically with these changes stashed at clean HEAD -- and lies on the lossy VarDCT path this work does not touch."
    state verified
    result pass
    method command
    observed_at git:2b7b5c0b8009e7cd220273cf621c72a5d3d9d4b0
    command "cargo test -p jpxl-encode --lib"
    summary """
        At 2b7b5c0 the jpxl-encode library suite is 122 passed, 0 failed, 0 ignored -- 117 pre-4G plus five gates this work added. bounded_budget_is_a_noop_below_the_budget asserts that for every shipped effort level a frame inside the budget scores at the floor stride, including the exact boundary, so the plumbing cannot change output on sub-budget frames. bounded_budget_raises_the_stride_with_frame_size asserts the stride rises with frame size and that scored samples stay within the budget plus at most two partial rows -- slack that is a function of row cost, not frame area, which is the property that makes ranking cost frame-size-independent. a_zero_budget_falls_back_to_the_floor_stride pins the degenerate cases. empty_overrides_leave_every_effort_budget_untouched and each_override_replaces_only_its_own_lever pin the measurement escape hatch as inert by default. Separately verified: the one workspace failure, both_oracles_decode_a_stream_from_the_hf_mul_segment in jpxl-encode-policy/tests/vardct_oracle.rs, is pre-existing -- it fails identically with these changes stashed at clean HEAD -- and lies on the lossy VarDCT path this work does not touch.
        """
    author "GitHub Uploader"
}

record jpegxl-rs.evidence.phase4g-default-unchanged-2026-08-10/1 : evidence {
    title "At 2b7b5c0 the default effort is byte-identical on all three corpus sizes: small_0p8MP 1,075,465 B sha16 C3C60CEE4D0741D9, mid_4MP 5,157,974 B sha16 5C49AB9020706F0D, large_12MP 9,795,599 B sha16 CA27799D3E7B441D -- the same fingerprints the pre-effort-ramp encoder produced. The default short-circuits the search entirely (search_is_a_foregone_conclusion), so neither the sample-budget plumbing nor the cost-model unit fix can reach it. Effort 7 deliberately DOES change and now matches its own post-fix baseline: 1,037,868 B sha16 40F0DA161B8960FC (-3.5%), 4,942,547 B sha16 EAEC691E4AAF19C6 (-4.2%), and 9,795,599 B sha16 CA27799D3E7B441D unchanged at 12 MP. The pre-fix effort-7 fingerprints were retired on purpose: they encoded a search that could not see a winning split at any stride above 1."
