record jpegxl-rs.evidence.phase6-2-transpose-immaterial-2026-08-12/1 : evidence {
    title "The 6.0/6.1 coefficient-index transpose changes no result: the default square matrices are exactly symmetric"
    state verified
    result pass
    method command
    observed_at git:a015011c3d86727100e61f69d83d3a380b1d9888
    summary """
        idct2d_8x8 (used by Phases 6.0/6.1) and idct_2d_raw (I.7.3, the encoder's own convention via forward_dct_rc) are both orthonormal but differ by a transpose of the coefficient index; the I.2.5 default square dequant matrices were measured exactly symmetric (worst relative asymmetry 0.000000 for every channel at 8x8, 16x16 and 32x32), so 6.1 paired every cell with the correct step regardless, and only the u/v labels in the 6.0/6.1 tables are transposed
        """
}

