record jpegxl-rs.evidence.phase6-3-quality-screen-2026-08-12/1 : evidence {
    title "Phase 6.3 screen: frequency weighting helps at 1 bpp and hurts at 2 bpp, exactly as the failed agreement check predicts"
    state verified
    result pass
    method observation
    observed_at git:7e2b03759e368199cd0856aa824ec80e10170a99
    artifact "JPXL/docs/experiments/2026-08-12-csf-frequency-weight.md"
    summary """
        The screen ran and decided; the Contract B promotion gate fails but the result is a rate-split mis-calibration, not a null. Across 14 exactly-matched-rate cells the split is sharp: at 1 bpp butteraugli improves in 5 of 7 (mean -2.20%, best -16.4%) and SSIMULACRA2 improves in 7 of 7 (mean +1.22, best +4.37); at 2 bpp butteraugli regresses in 5 of 7 (mean +13.10%, worst +32.4%) and SSIMULACRA2 in 6 of 7. Two 2-bpp cells undershoot the cap by about 4.2%, inflating that mean by roughly a point without changing direction. Production remains CoverFrequencyWeight::Flat
        """
}

record jpegxl-rs.evidence.phase6-3-scorer-recomputation-2026-08-12/1 : evidence {
    title "The scorer applies the published CSF table per transform, mean-1, lambda left calibrated"
    state verified
    result pass
    method command
    observed_at git:7e2b03759e368199cd0856aa824ec80e10170a99
    command "cargo test -p jpxl-encode-policy --lib the_csf_weight_matches_a_direct_recomputation_of_the_weighted_term"
    summary """
        For each of DCT8x8, DCT16x16 and DCT32x32 the table the scorer reads matches csf::square_weights cell for cell to 1e-6 on that transform's own grid, its mean over the non-LLF cells is 1 to 1e-5 (the property that leaves HfQuantizers::lambda calibrated, so the weight moves only the distribution across frequency and not the rate/distortion balance), and the flat policy publishes no table at all; csf module tests separately pin the model as band-pass with its peak in 5..12 cycles/degree and the weights as falling from the low band to the corner at every size
        """
}

