record jpegxl-rs.evidence.phase6-5-quality-screen-2026-08-12/1 : evidence {
    title "Phase 6.5 screen: prediction confirmed, best result on the track, Contract B still not cleared"
    state verified
    result pass
    method observation
    observed_at git:286ad71af4f3f732adadcb7776d918a7b3d8f08b
    artifact "JPXL/docs/experiments/2026-08-12-quant-donor-frequency-weight.md"
    summary """
        28 exactly-matched-rate cells (7 test-set photographs at 0.5/1/2/4 bpp, donor encoded to the flat arm's achieved byte count, both decoded with the pinned djxl). Pooled: butteraugli better in 17 of 28, mean -0.17%; SSIMULACRA2 better in 18 of 28, mean +1.37. By rate: 0.5 bpp butteraugli 5/7 better (mean -4.89%, best -12.3%) with SSIMULACRA2 better on all 7 (mean +4.85); 1 bpp butteraugli 4/7 (mean -1.86%) with SSIMULACRA2 7/7 (mean +0.70); 2 bpp mean +6.74% but median -0.03%, the mean carried by two outliers at already-excellent absolute quality (s2/2 +30.7% on butteraugli 1.6885, s5/2 +24.7% on 1.1264); 4 bpp effectively a no-op (mean -0.69%, most cells within 0.1%). The pre-registered prediction is CONFIRMED: the 2 bpp arm halved from Phase 6.3's +13.10% mean to +6.74%, as the high-frequency pricing improvement from 0.41x to 0.65x of target predicted. Contract B still fails (11 of 28 cells regress on butteraugli), so production remains CoverFrequencyWeight::Flat
        """
}

record jpegxl-rs.evidence.phase6-5b-promotion-equivalence-2026-08-12/1 : evidence {
    title "The promoted default reproduces the screened donor arm exactly on all 7 scenes; new production fingerprint recorded"
    state verified
    result pass
    method observation
    observed_at git:48d5acd8d00a7caea8e814d6895bee2f75fdb0f2
    artifact ".agent/scratch/phase6-5-quant-donor-2026-08-12/promotion-verify.txt"
    summary """
        Encoding each of the 7 corpus scenes with the promoted default at that scene's screened byte cap reproduces the Phase 6.5 donor arm EXACTLY on all 7 -- identical byte count and identical rmse, psnr, ssimulacra2, butteraugli and butteraugli_pnorm3. The promotion is therefore the screened configuration itself rather than something merely similar, which is a stronger confirmation than a fresh comparative run would give. The new target-rate production fingerprint for test-set/20240501_110934 at 1 bpp is 98,136 bytes, SSIMULACRA2 63.5625, butteraugli 4.8887 (rmse 8.063372, psnr 30.0005), superseding the 97,539 bytes / 62.5738 / 5.0325 baseline cited by Phases 6.2b, 6.3 and 6.5; note the new figure is measured at --bpp 1 independently rather than at a shared cap, so it sits 0.61% above the old byte count and is not itself a matched-rate comparison -- the matched evidence is the 28-cell screen
        """
}

